000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. DECLAR.
000300* A USE procedure is not called by the program: the I-O system
000400* calls it. General rule 1 on IV-32 says it runs on the AT END
000500* condition when the READ carried no AT END phrase of its own,
000600* and general rule 2 says control returns to the invoking
000700* routine afterwards -- which is exactly a PERFORM range.
000800* Syntax rule 3 keeps control from crossing into or out of the
000900* declaratives, so they are branched around.
001000 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
001100 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001200 FILE-CONTROL.
001300     SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-INFILE.
001400 DATA DIVISION.
001500 FILE SECTION.
001600 FD  IN-FILE
001700     LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
001800 01  IN-REC.
001850     02  IN-KEY   PIC X(20).
001880     02  FILLER   PIC X(60).
001900 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002000 01  DECL-COUNT   PIC 9      VALUE 0.
002100 01  READ-COUNT   PIC 9      VALUE 0.
002200 01  EOF-FLAG     PIC X      VALUE 'N'.
002300 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
002400 DECLARATIVES.
002500 EOF-HANDLER SECTION.
002600     USE AFTER STANDARD EXCEPTION PROCEDURE ON IN-FILE.
002700 NOTE-THE-END.
002800     ADD 1 TO DECL-COUNT.
002900     MOVE 'Y' TO EOF-FLAG.
003000 END DECLARATIVES.
003100 MAIN SECTION.
003200 MAIN-START.
003300     DISPLAY 'START'.
003400     OPEN INPUT IN-FILE.
003500     PERFORM READ-ONE UNTIL EOF-FLAG = 'Y'.
003600     CLOSE IN-FILE.
003700     DISPLAY 'READS  ' READ-COUNT.
003800     DISPLAY 'DECLS  ' DECL-COUNT.
003900     STOP RUN.
004000 READ-ONE.
004100     READ IN-FILE.
004200     IF EOF-FLAG NOT = 'Y'
004300         ADD 1 TO READ-COUNT
004400         DISPLAY 'REC    ' IN-KEY.
